# --- Native build artifacts -------------------------------------------------
# Compiled binaries. Note the `microgpt-*` pattern also covers the per-config
# names tools/parity.py builds (microgpt-micro, microgpt-scaled).
microgpt
microgpt-*
test_gradients
/go/*
!/go/go.mod
/go.sum
# Rust
implementations/rust/target/
# The tuned candidate is a second Rust crate and needs its own line here, or
# `git add` in the research loop sweeps 200 MB of build output into a commit.
autoresearch/candidate/target/
# The Go candidate's built binaries. A build product of a directory a model can
# edit, exactly like the Rust candidate's target/, and for the same reason: it
# would be 2.5 MB of machine-specific object code in every commit.
#
# Two names, because two different invocations produce them: `build_track` writes
# `microgpt-go` (it names the output), and a bare `go build ./...` in a module
# whose directory is `go` writes a file called `go`. Both have shown up.
autoresearch/candidate-go/microgpt-go
autoresearch/candidate-go/go
# Go coverage / test binaries
*.test
# C
*.o
*.d
*.profraw
*.gcda
*.gcno
# Checkpoints written by the C implementation
model.bin
*.bin.tmp

# Raw tool output. The parsed traces/*.jsonl are committed; the stdout they were
# parsed from is build output, and keeping both means the drift check has two
# things to disagree about.
traces/**/stdout.txt
.run/

# --- Autoresearch -----------------------------------------------------------
# The unedited model response behind each experiment. The parsed record is
# committed in autoresearch/runs/*.json; this is the raw text, which is only
# interesting when a session is going wrong.
autoresearch/logs/

